From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:41:29 +0900
Subject: A prompt in the session bus of its requester: a delegate shows it
 there
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

polkit picks one agent per login session, but a session can have more than one desktop: a nested
or headless compositor with a session bus of its own. Rungic's independent desktop (workspace 0,
docs/research/97 §19) is a KWin and a bus of its own inside the phone's session; polkit sends its
apps' requests to the phone session's agent, which drew the dialog on the phone, portrait and in
the phone's look, while the desktop is landscape (on the phone's fullscreen, a TV or a remote
viewer).

The agent polkit knows (the router) now reads the requesting process's DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
(polkit.subject-pid, /proc/<pid>/environ). When it is another socket of this user in its
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, the request goes to org.kde.Polkit1AuthAgent.Delegate on that bus (Begin, then
Finished; Cancel when polkit cancels; the delegate gone ends the request with an error). The
delegate is this program with --delegate, D-Bus activatable on that bus, not registered with
polkit: PolicyKitListener shows the dialog as before, with an async result of its own, and
polkit-agent-helper-1 checks the password with the request's cookie (polkit only checks that the
helper's caller is the agent's user). Its Prompting property says a request waits there. Requests
whose bus is the router's own, unreadable or not acceptable, or whose delegate cannot be reached,
get the router's dialog as before.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [one login session with several compositors and session buses]
X-Rungic-Tests: L1:routetest; L3:docs/research/97 §21.7
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/research/97 §21
